          <items xsi:type="form:FormField">
            <name>NodeAccountingOption</name>
            <id>486</id>
            <title>
              <key>en</key>
              <value>Sub-assets</value>
            </title>
            <title>
              <key>fa</key>
              <value>زیردارایی‌ها</value>
            </title>
            <title>
              <key>ru</key>
              <value>Узлы</value>
            </title>
            <title>
              <key>tr</key>
              <value>Alt üniteler</value>
            </title>
            <title>
              <key>it</key>
              <value>Sub-assets</value>
            </title>
            <title>
              <key>pl</key>
              <value>Sub-assets</value>
            </title>
            <title>
              <key>vi</key>
              <value>Sub-assets</value>
            </title>
            <visible>true</visible>
            <enabled>true</enabled>
            <userVisible>
              <common>true</common>
            </userVisible>
            <dataPath xsi:type="form:DataPath">
              <segments>NodeAccountingOption</segments>
            </dataPath>
            <titleHeight>2</titleHeight>
            <toolTipRepresentation>Button</toolTipRepresentation>
            <handlers>
              <event>OnChange</event>
              <name>OptionForAccountingForComponentNodesONChange</name>
            </handlers>
            <extendedTooltip>
              <name>NodeAccountingOptionExtendedTooltip</name>
              <id>488</id>
              <title>
                <key>en</key>
                <value>If &lt;b>Write off&lt;/> option is selected, the cost and depreciation of sub-assets will be included in the fixed asset.
The total cost of fixed assets for recognition must be equal to the cost of the original fixed asset, including the cost of sub-assets and depreciation components.

If the &lt;b>Leave in accounting&lt;/> option is selected, there will be no changes in sub-assets of the fixed asset.
In this case, you need to decide what to do with them, for example, they can be transferred to fixed assets obtained during splitting.
The total cost of fixed assets for recognition must be equal to the cost of the original fixed asset, including the cost of depreciation components.

Depreciation components are always written off (the cost and depreciation will be included in the fixed asset).
</value>
              </title>
              <title>
                <key>fa</key>
                <value>اگر گزینه &lt;b>اسقاط&lt;/> انتخاب شود، بهای تمام‌شده و استهلاک دارایی‌های فرعی در دارایی ثابت گنجانده خواهد شد.
بهای کل دارایی‌های ثابت برای شناسایی باید برابر با بهای دارایی ثابت اولیه، شامل بهای دارایی‌های فرعی و اجزای استهلاک باشد.

اگر گزینه &lt;b>باقی ماندن در حسابداری&lt;/> انتخاب شود، تغییری در دارایی‌های فرعی دارایی ثابت ایجاد نخواهد شد.
در این صورت، باید درباره آن‌ها تصمیم بگیرید، برای مثال، می‌توانند به دارایی‌های ثابت حاصل از تفکیک منتقل شوند.
بهای کل دارایی‌های ثابت برای شناسایی باید برابر با بهای دارایی ثابت اولیه، شامل بهای اجزای استهلاک باشد.

اجزای استهلاک همیشه اسقاط می‌شوند (بهای تمام‌شده و استهلاک در دارایی ثابت گنجانده خواهد شد).
</value>
              </title>
              <title>
                <key>ru</key>
                <value>Если выбран вариант &lt;b>Списать&lt;/>, то стоимость и амортизация узлов будет включена в основное средство-владельца.
Общая стоимость, принимаемых к учету ОС должна равняться стоимости исходного ОС с учетом стоимости узлов и компонентов амортизации.

Если выбран вариант &lt;b>Оставить в учете&lt;/>, то по узлам основного средства не будет никаких изменений.
В этом случае нужно самостоятельно решить, что с ними делать, например, их можно перенести на основные средства, полученные при разукомплектации.
Общая стоимость, принимаемых к учету ОС должна равняться стоимости исходного ОС с учетом стоимости компонентов амортизации.

Компоненты амортизации всегда списываются (стоимость и амортизация будет включена в основное средство-владельца).
</value>
              </title>
              <title>
                <key>tr</key>
                <value>&lt;b>Sil&lt;/> seçeneği seçilirse, alt ünitelerin maliyeti ve amortismanı ana sabit kıymete dahil edilir.
Muhasebeleştirilecek sabit kıymetlerin toplam maliyeti, alt ünitelerin ve amortisman unsurlarının maliyeti dikkate alınarak orijinal sabit kıymetin maliyetine eşit olmalıdır.

 &lt;b>Kayıtlarda tut&lt;/> seçeneği seçilirse, sabit kıymet bileşenlerinde hiçbir değişiklik yapılmaz.
Bu durumda onlarla ne yapılacağına kendiniz karar vermelisiniz; örneğin, sökümden elde edilen sabit kıymetlere aktarılabilirler.
Muhasebeleştirilecek sabit kıymetlerin toplam maliyeti, amortisman bileşenlerinin maliyeti dikkate alınarak orijinal sabit kıymetin maliyetine eşit olmalıdır.

Amortisman bileşenleri her zaman silinir (maliyet ve amortisman ana sabit kıymete dahil edilir).
</value>
              </title>
              <title>
                <key>it</key>
                <value>If &lt;b>Write off&lt;/> option is selected, the cost and depreciation of sub-assets will be included in the fixed asset.
The total cost of fixed assets for recognition must be equal to the cost of the original fixed asset, including the cost of sub-assets and depreciation components.

If the &lt;b>Leave in accounting&lt;/> option is selected, there will be no changes in sub-assets of the fixed asset.
In this case, you need to decide what to do with them, for example, they can be transferred to fixed assets obtained during splitting.
The total cost of fixed assets for recognition must be equal to the cost of the original fixed asset, including the cost of depreciation components.

Depreciation components are always written off (the cost and depreciation will be included in the fixed asset).
</value>
              </title>
              <title>
                <key>pl</key>
                <value>If &lt;b>Write off&lt;/> option is selected, the cost and depreciation of sub-assets will be included in the fixed asset.
The total cost of fixed assets for recognition must be equal to the cost of the original fixed asset, including the cost of sub-assets and depreciation components.

If the &lt;b>Leave in accounting&lt;/> option is selected, there will be no changes in sub-assets of the fixed asset.
In this case, you need to decide what to do with them, for example, they can be transferred to fixed assets obtained during splitting.
The total cost of fixed assets for recognition must be equal to the cost of the original fixed asset, including the cost of depreciation components.

Depreciation components are always written off (the cost and depreciation will be included in the fixed asset).
</value>
              </title>
              <title>
                <key>vi</key>
                <value>If &lt;b>Write off&lt;/> option is selected, the cost and depreciation of sub-assets will be included in the fixed asset.
The total cost of fixed assets for recognition must be equal to the cost of the original fixed asset, including the cost of sub-assets and depreciation components.

If the &lt;b>Leave in accounting&lt;/> option is selected, there will be no changes in sub-assets of the fixed asset.
In this case, you need to decide what to do with them, for example, they can be transferred to fixed assets obtained during splitting.
The total cost of fixed assets for recognition must be equal to the cost of the original fixed asset, including the cost of depreciation components.

Depreciation components are always written off (the cost and depreciation will be included in the fixed asset).
</value>
              </title>
              <formatted>true</formatted>
              <type>Label</type>
              <autoMaxWidth>true</autoMaxWidth>
              <autoMaxHeight>true</autoMaxHeight>
              <extInfo xsi:type="form:LabelDecorationExtInfo">
                <horizontalAlign>Left</horizontalAlign>
              </extInfo>
            </extendedTooltip>
